    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Initialize thicknesses from round-7 best candidate [32.0, 252.0, 24.0, 218.0, 31.0, 259.0, 33.0, 253.0, 26.0, 247.0, 24.0, 266.0, 23.0, 269.0, 22.0, 256.0, 23.0, 248.0, 25.0, 262.0, 24.0, 252.0, 21.0, 233.0, 21.0, 244.0, 30.0, 269.0, 31.0, 236.0, 22.0, 235.0, 23.0, 235.0, 29.0, 29.0] nm, then apply asymmetric offset: add +8 nm to odd-indexed layers (indices 0,2,4,...,34) and subtract 8 nm from even-indexed layers (indices 1,3,5,...,35). Clamp all thicknesses to 20-350 nm bounds. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with step size multiplier 0.5x. Optimize for: maximize transmittance in 420-700 nm band, minimize transmittance in 354-356 nm band, minimize transmittance in 355-365 nm band, minimize transmittance in 1030-1080 nm band. Wavelength grid: 300-1200 nm with 1 nm resolution. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
